From 49877da88d4327238e7ace0ece3c74a69c8a4e09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thet Naing <thet@brightwave.io>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:40:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(code): keep pull request state live on the PR page

The detail pane loaded once and then ignored the live summary row, so
checks finishing, merges landing, and new comments never appeared
without a manual refresh. "Checking status" never resolved on its own:
GitHub computes mergeability lazily and nothing ever asked again.
Actions repainted only after a full round trip, and a merge could
repaint backwards off a stale read replica.

The pane now re-reads when the row's live signature moves, polls on a
short backoff while mergeability is unknown, paints a settled action's
outcome immediately and holds it over stale host reads, and names the
in-flight action in the gate headline. The workspace PR read kicks one
detached host refresh when the stored digest still answers unknown, so
the workspace chip clears in seconds instead of a hot-tier tick.
